,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,37175,279,52484,8500,57960,37018,90,16,17,20,15170,24,2137,1124,37018,90,17,20,15170,18,2137,220,20,11,220,18,11,1124,507,2412,12947,3555,374,279,36377,4647,315,279,8500,30,17399,697,4226,438,264,4185,19419,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nConsider the geometric sequence $\\frac{125}{9}, \\frac{25}{3}, 5, 3, \\ldots$. What is the eighth term of the sequence? Express your answer as a common fraction.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"f38a735cb0679aa530b92f062a11210b46d375db8b9e78b554eb9be324fecf0b"},"seconds":50.20171046257019,"seed":612501518747050843,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the eighth term of the geometric sequence given as $\\frac{125}{9}, \\frac{25}{3}, 5, 3, \\ldots$, we follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the first term and the common ratio:**\n\n   The first term of the sequence is $a_1 = \\frac{125}{9}$.\n   \n   To find the common ratio $r$, we divide the second term by the first term:\n   \\[\n   r = \\frac{\\frac{25}{3}}{\\frac{125}{9}} = \\frac{25}{3} \\times \\frac{9}{125} = \\frac{25 \\times 9}{3 \\times 125} = \\frac{225}{375} = \\frac{3}{5}.\n   \\]\n\n2. **General formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of a geometric sequence:**\n\n   The \\(n\\)-th term of a geometric sequence can be found using the formula:\n   \\[\n   a_n = a_1 \\cdot r^{n-1}.\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the eighth term \\(a_8\\):**\n\n   Substitute \\(a_1 = \\frac{125}{9}\\), \\(r = \\frac{3}{5}\\), and \\(n = 8\\) into the formula:\n   \\[\n   a_8 = \\frac{125}{9} \\cdot \\left( \\frac{3}{5} \\right)^{8-1} = \\frac{125}{9} \\cdot \\left( \\frac{3}{5} \\right)^7.\n   \\]\n\n4. **Simplify the expression:**\n\n   First, calculate \\(\\left( \\frac{3}{5} \\right)^7\\):\n   \\[\n   \\left( \\frac{3}{5} \\right)^7 = \\frac{3^7}{5^7} = \\frac{2187}{78125}.\n   \\]\n\n   Now, multiply this by \\(\\frac{125}{9}\\):\n   \\[\n   a_8 = \\frac{125}{9} \\cdot \\frac{2187}{78125} = \\frac{125 \\cdot 2187}{9 \\cdot 78125}.\n   \\]\n\n5. **Simplify the fraction:**\n\n   Simplify the numerator and the denominator:\n   \\[\n   125 \\cdot 2187 = 273375,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   9 \\cdot 78125 = 703125.\n   \\]\n\n   So,\n   \\[\n   a_8 = \\frac{273375}{703125}.\n   \\]\n\n   Simplify the fraction by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 273375 and 703125. The GCD is 273375, so:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{273375}{703125} = \\frac{273375 \\div 273375}{703125 \\div 273375} = \\frac{1}{2.57142857143} \\approx \\frac{1}{2.57142857143} = \\frac{1}{3}.\n   \\]\n\nSo, the eighth term of the sequence is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{27}{125}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{27}{125}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
